 # Stageshow
 
 Miniature product UI: a believable interface, framed in its space, as one still or a short animation in which one thing happens. The viewer recognizes the screen and sees the thing happen.
 
+## OMP scope
+
+Follow session and project rules and the authorized task scope. Discuss the design before editing until the user supplies `GO` or explicitly authorizes implementation. Reviews are read-only. Package installation, new documentation, commits, and remote mutations require their applicable explicit authorization.
+
+Resolve [Stageshow](skill://stageshow) for its installed filesystem location. Paths beginning with `references/`, `examples/`, `kit/`, `scripts/`, `assets/`, and `teaching/` are relative to that location; bare reference filenames are relative to `skill://stageshow/references/`. Keep the installed skill and upstream checkout unchanged. Copy the needed sources, assets, and license notices into the authorized project; use a project-local copy of the complete skill when the standalone playground is needed. Run the shell commands below from that working copy.
+
+Reuse the project's components, design decisions, and installed dependencies. Check available tools and global mise configuration before requesting missing packages. Use OMP browser or desktop tools for runtime evidence. Start preview servers through a named service, keep them local, and stop services you started when finished. Preserve the film gates, accessibility checks, and error handling; report unavailable checks and actual failures accurately.
+
 ## The one idea
 
 **It reads as a real product, simplified to what the viewer needs, framed with intent, and every motion has a cause.**
